The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls this one known issue with one queued fix.
Its own rendered cause table shows two mechanisms. The parser fix alone cannot correct the booking form's hint.
The findings below describe the supplied export. The later engineering update supplies the closure outcomes;
the export counts remain a historical snapshot rather than a live queue count.

<Callout kind="warn">
  Keep parser and form-hint work separate. A matching subject line, an intake tag, or the word “known”
  does not prove that two reports need the same fix. The desk closed the two mechanisms with different outcomes.
</Callout>

## Engineering update and closure

After the first submission, the [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows)
reported that #4471 closed on **5 October**:

- **Parser — fixed.** The engineering change is `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  The [parser issue](https://github.com/victorwhite5/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) is closed as completed.
- **Hint — won't fix.** Engineering retired the booking-v3 form rather than implementing a hint correction.
  The [hint issue](https://github.com/victorwhite5/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) is closed as not planned.

These are the desk's reported outcomes, preserved in `evidence/desk-update.json`.
This review did not independently test production. Retirement is not a shipped hint fix, and completing
the triage documentation alone was not sufficient evidence for closing both issues as completed.

